{"id":405,"flavor":[{"games":["Legends: Arceus"],"text":"They form packs, each having one male as leader. Legends say that when Luxray's two eyes shimmer with gold, the Pokémon can see through anything."},{"games":["Shield"],"text":"Seeing through solid objects uses up a lot of Luxray’s electricity, so the Pokémon sleeps for long periods of time to store up energy."},{"games":["Sword"],"text":"Luxray can see through solid objects. It will instantly spot prey trying to hide behind walls, even if the walls are thick."},{"games":["Alpha Sapphire","Y","SoulSilver","HeartGold"],"text":"Luxray’s ability to see through objects comes in handy when it’s scouting for danger."},{"games":["Omega Ruby","X","Pearl"],"text":"When its eyes gleam gold, it can spot hiding prey—even those taking shelter behind a wall."},{"games":["White 2","Black 2","White","Black","Platinum"],"text":"It can see clearly through walls to track down its prey and seek its lost young."},{"games":["Diamond"],"text":"It has eyes that can see through anything. It spots and captures prey hiding behind objects."}],"abilities":[{"name":"Rivalry","hidden":false,"description":"The Pokémon's competitive spirit makes it deal more damage to Pokémon of the same gender, but less damage to Pokémon of the opposite gender."},{"name":"Intimidate","hidden":false,"description":"When the Pokémon enters a battle, it intimidates opposing Pokémon and makes them cower, lowering their Attack stats."},{"name":"Guts","hidden":true,"description":"It's so gutsy that having a status condition boosts the Pokémon's Attack stat."}],"eggGroups":["Field"],"genderRate":4,"hatchCounter":20,"baseHappiness":70,"growthRate":"medium slow","habitat":null,"color":"Blue","shape":"Quadruped","evolution":{"id":403,"name":"Shinx","condition":null,"children":[{"id":404,"name":"Luxio","condition":"Lv. 15","children":[{"id":405,"name":"Luxray","condition":"Lv. 30","children":[]}]}]},"moves":{"game":"Scarlet / Violet","level":[[1,33],[1,43],[1,84],[1,268]